-- ============================================================================
-- 27: render-replica LIVE — PHASE 3 HUD (health/timer/round/meter/combo) FOREGROUND.
-- The bodies + stage were on screen but the match had no HUD. This adds the MVC2 HUD
-- as a 2D foreground pass over the WebGPU canvas, every field grounded in the engine
-- state + the production GSTA wire's own addresses. (feat/render-replica-live.)
-- Pinned 2026-06-13.
-- ============================================================================
USE NS re DB kb;

UPSERT source:hud_field_addresses SET kind='code',
  ref='core/network/maplecast_gamestate.cpp (readState) + docs/MVC2-MEMORY-MAP.md page 649',
  note='The HUD field addresses are the SAME ones the SHIPPED production GSTA wire reads verbatim, so they are confirmed-live, not guessed. PER-CHAR (char-struct base + off): health +0x420 (u8), red_health/chip +0x424 (u8), char_id +0x001 (u8), active +0x000 (u8). GLOBAL (page 649): in_match 0x8C289624, round_counter 0x8C28962B, game_timer 0x8C289630, stage_id 0x8C289638, p1_meter_fill u16 0x8C289646, p2_meter_fill u16 0x8C289648, p1_meter_level u8 0x8C28964A, p2_meter_level u8 0x8C28964B, p1_combo u16 0x8C289670, p2_combo u16 0x8C289672. CONSTANTS: HP_MAX=144 (0x90); METER_MAX=144 (cited loc_8C0F0FDC meter_fill/144.0). The on-screen POINT char of a side is whichever of its 3 slots (P1={0,2,4}, P2={1,3,5}) has active!=0; its health/red_health drive that side life bar. Per-team life-bar gradient (which of C1/C2/C3 is active point -> magenta/green/cyan -> yellow) = the team-slot modulate loc_8c15FFB0.';

UPSERT source:hud_readset SET kind='code',
  ref='core/network/maplecast_replica_live.cpp buildTables()',
  note='The stage agent added D(0x8C289620, 0x20, "gstate") = 0x289620..0x28963F (in_match/round/timer/stage_id) but that 32B window does NOT reach the HUD meter (0x289646..0x64B) or combo (0x289670..0x673). EXTENDED to D(0x8C289620, 0x60, "gstate") = 0x289620..0x28967F so the SAME region now also carries p1/p2 meter_fill, meter_level, and combo. To reach combo (last byte 0x289673) the window must span 0x54 bytes; rounded to 0x60 (ends 0x28967F, still inside page 649). +0x40 bytes/frame on the wire, zstd-trivial (mostly stable). Per-char health/red_health/char_id already ride the "char_str" region (D(0x8C268340, 6*0x5A4, "char_str")) — no extra wire for them. NOTE: the server gstate extension deploys with the stage region in ONE batched headless rebuild (coordinated by the user) — built, not deployed independently.';

UPSERT source:hud_layout_reference SET kind='code',
  ref='web/webgpu/sprite-client.mjs drawHUD/_drawBar/_barCols/_pointSlot/_drawDigits',
  note='The faithful, already-grounded MVC2 HUD layout that the replay.html pass mirrors (640x480 game space): life bars LB={x1:18,x2:330,y:16,w:292,h:14} top-left(P1)/top-right(P2), red chip-damage (red_health/144) drawn FIRST then current HP (health/144) ON TOP so the chip trails BEHIND; P2 bars right-anchored (grow leftward). Super meters at (18,456,250,9)/(372,456,250,9) width=fill/144 team-tinted, right-anchored on P2. Meter-level pips 0..5 at y=446 (P1 left x=18+i*12, P2 right x=613-i*12). Round timer = 2 centered digits (game_timer 0..99) at (320, top). Combo counter per side (combo>1) top-corner. Colors = per-team gradient loc_8c15FFB0.';

UPSERT source:mvc2_hud_real_layout SET kind='reference',
  ref='arcadequartermaster.com/capcom/mvc2_controls.html + supercombo.gg Marvel_vs_Capcom_2/HUD + canonical in-match screenshots',
  note='REAL MVC2 in-match HUD geometry (the flat full-width bar was WRONG): TWO ANGLED (parallelogram) life bars swept toward screen center — P1 top-LEFT, P2 top-RIGHT (mirrored). Each is a SOLID BRIGHT team-color bar (magenta/green/cyan per active point char, NOT a rainbow gradient across the whole width) anchored at the OUTER (corner/portrait) end and DEPLETING toward CENTER; recoverable red chip-damage (red_health, dark red) TRAILS BEHIND the bright current-HP edge. Vitality = 144 points (HP_MAX). A portrait/name plate sits at each bar OUTER end; round/win star pips near it. Round TIMER centered at top between the two bars (2 digits, 99 marvel-seconds). HYPER COMBO GAUGE in the LOWER corners (P1 lower-left / P2 lower-right), stocks up to 5 levels/blocks with a numeric level indicator, filling from the outer corner inward. METER_MAX=144.';

UPSERT finding:replica_live_hud SET
  statement='PHASE 3 HUD landed on the render-replica LIVE client as a FOREGROUND pass over the bodies + stage, every field grounded in the engine state + the production GSTA wire addresses, NO model. web/render-replica/replay.html: renderHudPass() draws on a SEPARATE 2D overlay canvas layered exactly over the WebGPU body canvas (same technique as the quad-bounds overlay), called AFTER pane.render() in BOTH the file path (showFrame) and the live path (liveApplyFrame). It reads HUD state from the RAM image at the engine addresses (readHud()/hudPointSlot()): per-char health+0x420 / red_health+0x424 / active+0x000 / char_id+0x001 (from the shipped char_str region), globals in_match/timer/round/stage_id + meter_fill/meter_level/combo (from the EXTENDED gstate region). Render: life bars (chip-damage trailing behind current HP, team-gradient tint), super meters (fill/144), meter-level pips, round timer + per-side combo as 7-segment vector digits (built-in, no external art for v1 — fully local, dependency-free). Layout mirrors the grounded reference sprite-client.mjs drawHUD (loc_8c15FFB0 team gradient, loc_8C0F0FDC METER_MAX=144, HP_MAX=144). Server: core/network/maplecast_replica_live.cpp gstate region extended 0x20 -> 0x60 to cover meter+combo+P2. Body render (render_frame.wasm/gen_*.c/body_decoder.mjs), the stage pass, and the GFX/palette tails UNTOUCHED. Cache-bust ?v=stage1 -> ?v=hud1.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-13';

UPSERT finding:replica_live_hud_validated SET
  statement='The HUD foreground pass is PROVEN to reflect live state + match the MVC2 layout. Headless validation (tools/render-replica-poc/shot_hud.mjs, puppeteer WebGPU, real recording maxq_86.mcrr): STEP 1 __readHud() reads correct fields straight from the seeded RAM image (inMatch=1, timer=99, round=2, P1+P2 point slots active) — field plumbing confirmed on real recording bytes. STEP 2 drives grounded synthetic values (P1 HP 72/144 with chip to 110/144, P2 HP 130/144, P1 meter full / P2 half, level pips, timer 73, P1 combo 7) into the RAM image at the real engine addresses, re-runs renderHudPass(), and reads back the overlay: ALL 7 elements render (10585 non-blank px) — P1/P2 life bars (bright team-color HP fill), the red chip-damage trailing BEHIND current HP, P1/P2 super meters, the timer digits, the combo digits. Screenshot PNG_hud.png shows the composited HUD over the bodies/stage in the MVC2 layout (life bars top-L/top-R, timer center-top, meters/pips bottom). The body canvas reads back as the magenta clear-color under headless software WebGPU (known readback limitation, same as shot_replay.mjs) but the 2D HUD overlay reads back perfectly — confirming the foreground pass composites on top. LIVE meter/combo bytes require the batched headless rebuild (the extended gstate region) which the user coordinates; the layout/render/health-bar+timer path validate against the pre-extension recording today.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-13';

UPSERT finding:replica_live_hud_angled_layout SET
  statement='LAYOUT FIX (supersedes the flat-bar layout in finding:replica_live_hud): the HUD was drawing a WRONG full-width green->yellow->magenta team-gradient bar across the top (the gradient filled the WHOLE bar regardless of HP, so it looked like a rainbow that never depleted). Rewrote ONLY renderHudPass() in web/render-replica/replay.html to the REAL MVC2 layout, grounded in the in-match HUD reference (source:mvc2_hud_real_layout): TWO ANGLED (parallelogram) corner life bars via new helper hudAngledLifeBar() — P1 top-LEFT outer X=80, P2 top-RIGHT outer X=560 (mirror), LB_LEN=212, LB_H=15, LB_SKEW=26 sweep toward center; SOLID bright team color (HUD_BAR_COLS[colIdx][0], magenta/green/cyan — NOT a gradient) anchored at the OUTER end and DEPLETING toward center (fill from outer = hp(slot)); dark-red chip (#8a1414, red_health/144) drawn FIRST then bright HP ON TOP inside a shared parallelogram clip so the chip TRAILS BEHIND; white outline frame. Portrait/name plate (char_id digits) + 5-point win-star pips (round_counter) at each OUTER end. Centered TIMER (305,6 box, digits at 320). BOTTOM super meters via sheared meter() helper — P1 lower-left outer X=20 / P2 lower-right outer X=620, MT_LEN=200, MT_SKEW=16, fill/144 team color from outer corner inward, with level number + tick pips (0..5) above. Combo digits per side (combo>1). The chip color was darkened a01818->8a1414 so it reads as dark recoverable damage (max channel<140) distinct from bright HP. Cache-bust: title marker [hud:angled-v2] + renderHudPass header comment. UNTOUCHED: body render / stage pass / effects pass / GFX-palette tails (only renderHudPass + the hudBar/hudAngledLifeBar helper region changed).',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-13';

UPSERT finding:replica_live_hud_angled_validated SET
  statement='The angled HUD layout is PROVEN by a software-canvas geometry harness (tools/render-replica-poc/_hud_geom_check.cjs) that extracts the REAL renderHudPass()/hudAngledLifeBar()/hudDigits() verbatim from replay.html, runs them against a polygon-fill 2D-canvas shim with the SAME grounded synthetic state as shot_hud.mjs (P1 HP 72/144 chip-to-110, P2 130/144, P1 meter full lvl3, P2 half lvl1, timer73, P1 combo7), and samples the new geometry: ALL 7 elements render (10047 non-blank px) AND the two new MVC2-faithfulness assertions PASS — (a) the chip band TOP edge [186..241] is DARK red (lit but max-channel<140), proving HP depleted toward center with chip trailing; (b) the inner tip (x>=270) has NO magenta HP fill, proving HP anchors at the OUTER end and depletes toward center (not a full-width bar). Emits PNG_hud_geom.png (HUD over a dark backdrop): visually the two angled corner bars sweep toward center with a clear center gap, the timer is centered between them, the dark-red chip trails the half-depleted P1 bar, portrait/name plates + win stars at the outer ends, and the bottom super meters show fill + level pips — matching the MVC2 reference shape. shot_hud.mjs probe boxes were also re-aimed at the new angled coordinates for the headless WebGPU path (run when puppeteer is available). Full pixel-faithful headless WebGPU readback was not re-run here (puppeteer not installed in this env); the geometry/color/depletion contract is proven by the software-canvas harness instead.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-13';

UPSERT source:hud_real_art_source SET kind='reference',
  ref='MVC2 Dev Files/FONT.BIN (disc asset, gitignored) + tools/rip_hud_atlas.py + marvelous2 bank16/bank0f disasm',
  note='WHERE THE REAL HUD ART LIVES + HOW THE ENGINE DRAWS THE HUD. (1) DIGITS/FONT: FONT.BIN is a 2-record container (header stride 0x10, terminator 0xFFFF): rec0 @0x40 = 256x128 ARGB1555 TWIDDLED proportional font (A-Z a-z 0-9 + WINS/symbols); rec1 @0x10040 = 64x64 ARGB4444 TWIDDLED HUD glyph sheet = the BOXED digits 0-9 (4x4 16px cell grid, each cell rotated 90 CCW to upright) + EXP/LV gauge labels. tools/rip_hud_atlas.py decodes both, de-rotates+luminance-keys the 10 boxed digits, emits atlas/hud/hud_atlas.{png,json}. These boxed digits are the IN-MATCH timer + HIT/combo digits. (2) LIFE BAR + SUPER METER are NOT a distinct sprite: the engine draws a WHITE texel polygon MODULATED by a per-team-slot vertex color (bank15 loc_8c15FFB0, referenced from the in-match HUD dispatch table bank0f loc_8C0F06E0). So the faithful reconstruction is the team-tinted angled parallelogram (magenta/green/cyan per active point char C1/C2/C3) + the dark-red red_health chip trail, NOT an art asset. (3) The in-match HUD dispatch lives in bank0f (loc_8C0F06EC region; table at loc_8C0F06BC references char base 0x8C268340, the cell processor bank12 loc_8c1294C8, bank16 HUD draw routines loc_8c1604Ce/loc_8c1601B4, the bar modulate bank15 loc_8c15FFB0). The bank16 VITAL/TIME/COMPLETE/TOTAL #data tables (loc_8c160B54+) are RESULTS/stats-screen text layouts (glyph-index+color records into the FONT), NOT the in-match life bar. (4) PORTRAITS = PLxx_FAC.BIN (per-char, ~25-27KB, container header 0x0c000000 = offset table + compressed pixels) — deferred (tier 2). DISC inventory confirmed on dev box 65.109.77.178: FONT.BIN + PLxx_FAC.BIN present.';

UPSERT finding:replica_live_hud_real_art SET
  statement='SUPERSEDES the synthetic vector-digit HUD: the render-replica LIVE HUD now renders the GAME OWN art. New module web/render-replica/hud-client.mjs (class HudClient) loads ./hud/hud_atlas.{png,json} (FONT.BIN rec1 boxed-digit sprites via tools/rip_hud_atlas.py) and draws the TIMER + COMBO + meter-LEVEL with the real boxed-digit sprites (drawImage + source-atop tint), while the LIFE BAR + SUPER METER stay the engine-faithful procedural white-tex * per-slot vertex color (loc_8c15FFB0) angled team-tinted parallelogram + red_health chip trail (the engine does NOT use a distinct bar sprite — confirmed). replay.html renderHudPass() now delegates to HudClient.render(rdU8,rdU16,CHAR_SLOTS); the old synthetic renderer is retained DISABLED (_renderHudPassSynthDISABLED) only as the __readHud diagnostic source. Vector-digit fallback until the atlas async-loads. VALIDATED in real headless Chrome (tools/render-replica-poc/shot_hud_realart.mjs vs shot_hud_before.mjs): grounded synthetic state (P1 HP72/144 chip110, P2 130/144, P1 meter full lvl3, P2 half lvl1, timer73, P1 combo7) -> atlas LOADS (13 rects, src FONT.BIN), 15691 lit overlay px, the boxed game-font digits render in the timer/combo/level (vs the old flat 7-segment) -> before/after PNGs _atlas_out/PNG_hud_{before,realart}.png. DEPLOYED to prod 149.28.44.118 /var/www/maplecast/render-replica/ (replay.html + hud-client.mjs + hud/hud_atlas.{png,json}, all md5-verified == local; PROD title [hud:real-art-v1], hud-client.mjs?v=realart1 + atlas json/png all 200). ROM-derived hud_atlas.png is gitignored (scp-only); hud_atlas.json (pure layout coords) is committed. OPEN/tier-2: PLxx_FAC.BIN portraits (container decode), real character-name plates (FONT.BIN rec0 proportional font), exact in-match bar polygon vertices (would refine the angled geometry — defer to mvc2-sh4-re-expert bank0f/bank15 trace).',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

UPSERT finding:replica_live_hud_garble_fix SET
  statement='SUPERSEDES finding:replica_live_hud_real_art: the FONT.BIN real-art DIGIT path was the GARBLE SOURCE and is REMOVED. DIAGNOSIS (web/render-replica/hud/hud_atlas.{png,json} inspected pixel-by-pixel): the atlas contains NO magenta (0 magenta-ish pixels) — the pink/magenta is the engine team color #FF40FF (C1), which is CORRECT and clean. The actual garble was the DIGITS: the digit_0..9 atlas rects (x=0..169, y=0, 16x16) point at the EMPTY/fragmented top row (mostly (255,255,255,0) + stray white-with-varying-alpha glyph shards) — the real boxed digits live in the busy hud_sheet grid at y=146 (16x16 cells, dark/light box backgrounds that do NOT tint cleanly). _glyph() drew those white shards then source-atop tinted them -> noisy garbled digits. FIX (web/render-replica/hud-client.mjs [hud:clean-v1]): _glyph() now ALWAYS delegates to _vecDigit() (the clean 7-segment vector digit, re_kb-27 lineage) with a 1px dark halo for legibility; the FONT.BIN atlas digit drawImage/tint is DROPPED. load() is now best-effort (try/catch, never gates render) since the HUD is 100% procedural primitives — solid team-tinted angled life bars (HP depleting toward center + dark-red #8a1414 chip trail), sheared super meters + level pips, vector digits for timer/combo/level/char-id plates, win stars. Nothing textured remains, so nothing can garble. The angled-layout geometry (hudAngledLifeBar/meter, finding:replica_live_hud_angled_layout) is UNCHANGED. UNTOUCHED: body render/decode (render_frame.wasm/gen_*.c/body_decoder.mjs), stage pass, effects pass. Cache-bust: import ./hud-client.mjs?v=stagetex -> ?v=clean1, title [hud:real-art-v1] -> [hud:clean-v1].',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

UPSERT finding:replica_live_hud_garble_fix_validated SET
  statement='PROVEN CLEAN headless. tools/render-replica-poc/shot_hud.mjs (puppeteer WebGPU, real recording maxq_86.mcrr, grounded synthetic state: P1 HP72/144 chip110, P2 130/144, P1 meter full lvl3, P2 half lvl1, timer73, round2, P1 combo7): ALL 7 element checks PASS (11438 non-blank overlay px) — P1/P2 life bars, red chip trailing behind HP, P1/P2 super meters, timer digits, combo digits. Isolated HUD-overlay screenshot (HUD canvas composited over a neutral #202830 backing, _hud_only_shot.mjs -> PNG_hud_overlay_only.png) shows the HUD is FULLY CLEAN: crisp readable 7-segment timer "73", char-id plates "52"/"23" with win stars, combo "7", level pip + digit "3"/"1", solid magenta angled life bars (P1 half-depleted with dark-red chip band at the inner end, P2 right-anchored near-full), sheared super meters bottom — NO pink/magenta texture noise anywhere. NOTE: the FULL composited PNG_hud.png shows a magenta flood in the play area, but that is the WebGPU BODY canvas clear/readback under headless software-WebGPU (pre-existing, same limitation noted in finding:replica_live_hud_validated), NOT the HUD — the isolated overlay proves the HUD overlay is transparent everywhere except its own clean elements.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

RELATE finding:replica_live_hud_garble_fix->supersedes->finding:replica_live_hud_real_art;
RELATE finding:replica_live_hud_garble_fix->cites->source:hud_field_addresses;
RELATE finding:replica_live_hud_garble_fix->cites->source:mvc2_hud_real_layout;

RELATE finding:replica_live_hud_real_art->cites->source:hud_real_art_source;
RELATE finding:replica_live_hud_real_art->cites->source:hud_field_addresses;
RELATE finding:replica_live_hud_real_art->supersedes->finding:replica_live_hud_angled_layout;

RELATE finding:replica_live_hud->cites->source:hud_field_addresses;
RELATE finding:replica_live_hud->cites->source:hud_readset;
RELATE finding:replica_live_hud->cites->source:hud_layout_reference;
RELATE finding:replica_live_hud_validated->cites->source:hud_field_addresses;
RELATE finding:replica_live_hud_validated->cites->source:hud_layout_reference;
RELATE finding:replica_live_hud_angled_layout->cites->source:mvc2_hud_real_layout;
RELATE finding:replica_live_hud_angled_layout->cites->source:hud_field_addresses;
RELATE finding:replica_live_hud_angled_validated->cites->source:mvc2_hud_real_layout;
RELATE finding:replica_live_hud_angled_layout->supersedes->finding:replica_live_hud;
